<title>USA: California Jockey won't pay second half div.</title>
<headline>California Jockey won't pay second half div.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MATEO, Calif. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Jockey Club said on Wednesday it would not pay a dividend for the second half of 1996 because of reduced earnings.</p>
<p>The lower earnings are attributable to increased general and administrative costs and less than projected rent from racing facilities at Bay Meadows Racecourse, the company said.</p>
</text>
